{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":580998,"name":"","username":"manolo_automations","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/a9adbd/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-02T08:40:14.690Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi everyone \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twemoji/waving_hand.png?v=15\" title=\":waving_hand:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":waving_hand:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m an n8n automation developer available for freelance / project-based work, remote. I focus on building \u003cstrong\u003eproduction systems that actually run for real clients\u003c/strong\u003e — not disconnected demo workflows.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat I build:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnd-to-end n8n workflows connecting forms, Google Sheets, email (SMTP/Gmail) and SMS\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWebhook-driven automations (e.g. confirmation/cancellation buttons that update a live sheet in real time)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eScheduled workflows (reminders, reports) with filtering logic\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelf-hosted n8n setups on a VPS (Hetzner + reverse proxy)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGoogle OAuth / API integrations, error handling, and clear documentation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRecent real-world project — appointment \u0026amp; lead system for clinics:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nI designed and deployed a complete system for medical/beauty practices that:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCaptures every booking request via a form → logs it to the client’s own Google Sheet → sends instant email/SMS notifications to both the business and the customer\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSends automated next-day reminders with \u003cstrong\u003econfirm / cancel buttons\u003c/strong\u003e — when a patient clicks, the system writes the response back to the correct row and shows a thank-you page. This lets the business know in advance who’s coming and fill the gaps.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGenerates a monthly report (total requests, after-hours requests, reminders sent)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRuns fully self-hosted, data stays in the client’s own Google account, my access is revocable with one click\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEverything is tested node-by-node, timezone-correct, and documented so the client isn’t locked to me.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHow I work:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePer-project (fixed scope) — I’ll map your process first, then build around your actual flow\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFlexible availability, quick communication\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI care about reliability: correct triggers, working integrations, error handling, and post-launch support\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStack:\u003c/strong\u003e n8n · webhooks · REST APIs · Google Sheets/Gmail/OAuth · SMTP · SMS (HTTP API) · JavaScript expressions · self-hosted (Hetzner/Caddy)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you have a workflow you want built, fixed, or optimized, send me a message with a short description of your goal and current pain point — happy to discuss.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twemoji/envelope_with_arrow.png?v=15\" title=\":envelope_with_arrow:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":envelope_with_arrow:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e \u003ca href=\"mailto:giorgosmanolopoulos07@gmail.com\"\u003egiorgosmanolopoulos07@gmail.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twemoji/credit_card.png?v=15\" title=\":credit_card:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":credit_card:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e Payment via Wise\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks!\u003cbr\u003e\nGiorgos\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"p